{"id": "EUVD-2026-76611", "enisaUuid": "e12db468-d174-3ff7-9bfa-a812937aa38e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: validate symlink target length in NFSv4 CREATE\n\nnfsd4_decode_create() accepts an unbounded cr_datalen from the wire for\nNF4LNK symlink targets, allowing a client to force a kmalloc of up to\nthe maximum RPC payload size (several MiB) per COMPOUND op that persists\nuntil compound teardown.  The VFS rejects oversized targets with\nENAMETOOLONG, but the allocation has already occurred.\n\nReject cr_datalen == 0 early with nfserr_inval and cr_datalen greater\nthan NFS4_MAXPATHLEN (PATH_MAX) with nfserr_nametoolong to bound the\nallocation.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:12", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36011308b3f01ce7dc9954f3cefcbb5291af9f95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/888dad4b557352cf85be31613407b5ba51ad07d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8661d3cb38fd148947e57dbc0871fd4d3fa33bbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ef5e7a01a4d74995a65496bc9166d1e980a4355", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b24843ea3de1676b29902457b38507c95a80649b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/895a485cd3758031ef9993c0d53cf19ce8fb4ccc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45ec115cbfecb4b3cfab7fca6f73d1b60696a25a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/041f57056e5fb9c80adc088269322d2c61074406"], "aliases": ["GHSA-864v-pq9r-vg9w", "CVE-2026-89699"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.5, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04db715d-f4d9-39b9-be10-6f8e1f6750c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <041f57056e5fb9c80adc088269322d2c61074406"}, {"id": "0a2b46b0-9cd0-352d-8265-f6a60aeda4f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7